To address that gap we designed and implemented a 5-DOF manipulator prototype at Diponegoro University that fuses color and distance sensing to gate pick actions, uses a PCA9685 12-bit PWM driver to reduce MCU timing load, and separates power rails to avoid brownouts. Contributions are: 
• A sensor-fused control method that attains 95.4% color classification accuracy and F1 = 0.947 on a nine-box testbed while running on an Arduino Uno R3; 
• A PWM calibration and mapping procedure (with exact pulse tables) that yields repeatable placement with average cycle latency 12.3 ms and peak power draw 21 W; 
• A fault-handling and alert policy that rejects unrecognized colors, enforces per-color quotas (three items), and recovers from communication dropouts within 200 ms. These contributions are validated in ordered, randomized, and disturbance tests (50 runs each).
